WEBVTT

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.670
Erin.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:09.790
Mom!  Mom!

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:19.300
Jone the Honey Man

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.890
I've just returned.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.910
Ah, Nassan.  So how was Soyon doing?

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.650
She was executed by means of the Touda Trial.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.420
How could that be?!

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.630
Are you sure about this?

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:58.920
I saw it with my own eyes.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:08.180
Let us pray so that Soyon won't be lost on her way to the afterworld.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.830
Let us pray to our ancestors.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:15.910
She was such a wise girl, with a strong heart.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.130
Nassan.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.110
Explain in detail what happened in Ake Village.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:23.920
Yes.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:30.970
Shortly before Soyon's execution, all the Kiba died.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.930
Kiba are a precious treasure to the Grand Duke.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:39.250
To avoid the Grand Duke demanding accountability from the Inspector,

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.430
they blamed Soyon as the mastermind and executed her.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.700
What a terrible thing to do...

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:57.100
However, Soyon's daughter dove into the swamp in an attempt to save her.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:02.320
She must have been unable to stand the thought of her own child being eaten by Touda.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:08.220
Soyon used one of the skills of a Renditioner to save her daughter.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.740
What?!  A Renditioner skill?

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:15.780
We mustn't!  The skills a Renditioner possesses can't be revealed to others!

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.710
If word of our skills were to leak out...

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.490
Regarding that, the Inspector is a cowardly person.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:30.210
He doesn't want any negative records on his clean career, so he ordered the others not to tell anyone what they saw.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.420
Then there is no rumor about the Renditioner's skill?

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.200
None.  I'm sure it won't spread.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:45.760
Nassan.  The codes that were created and passed down by our ancestors must be protected at all costs.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.160
Catastrophe must never again be brought down on the world.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.240
Find where Soyon's daughter is now.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:59.630
The possible cause of a rumor must be taken care of.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.140
As you wish.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.170
It's fate for all mist to return to mist.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:35.780
The honey looks good this year, too.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.500
Let's check how the hive by the lake is doing.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.430
Why, excuse me.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.140
Looks like I will get some good honey from here, too.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.290
This scent...

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.520
Is it a Touda?!

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.510
No, it isn't.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.770
It's a child!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:52.720
Hey, are you okay?!

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.150
Get a hold of yourself!

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.400
Hey!  Hey, open your eyes!

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.880
Can you see me?!  Can you feel me?!

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.300
A bear?

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:11.130
Stay with me!

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.170
Does your back hurt?

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:25.580
Bear with me.  There isn't a bathtub big enough around here for me to put you in.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:30.070
First, I've got to get all of the mud off of you.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.440
I can't even tell if you're hurt or not.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.580
Erin.  It's shishi meat.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.100
Mom?

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:44.780
Mom!

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.780
Mom!  Run!

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.170
Sorry.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.010
Bees die when their stingers are pulled out.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:57.400
They are just small insects, but to Jone, every one of them was a treasure.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:03.210
But to cure Erin's injuries, he needed the bees' stingers.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:11.740
After making sure that Erin had never been stung by a bee before, he carefully used the bees' venom.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.330
What was that?

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:49.540
So you're awake.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.390
You can laugh, you know.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.600
A fart?

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:13.320
Listen.  It's better to fart than not to.

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:18.140
You're letting out the bad gas that's accumulated within you.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:25.800
If you don't fart, the gas bloats your stomach and lifts you up in the air, and eventually...

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:26.970
"boom" you go.

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:30.430
Seriously?

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.760
I'm just kidding.  Kidding.

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:38.550
They'd come out before you'd float away.

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:43.010
But I guess I don't want you laughing at me, so I should hold them in a bit from now on.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:52.450
Looks like your fever's down.

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:55.500
Your face looks much better.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.570
Does your body hurt at all?

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:00.360
I'm fine.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:04.120
Good.  At this rate, you should recover soon enough.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:14.440
A growling stomach is proof that your body is trying to get better.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.190
There, eat up.

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:21.910
You're a girl with strong luck.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:24.800
You came back from the riverbed of the afterworld.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:28.980
Anyways, all is well now!

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:34.960
Mom...

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:42.360
<i>Live.  And find your happiness. </i>

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.780
You shouldn't move yet!

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.230
Mom's bracelet!

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:04.820
I thought it'd be in your way while you were sleeping.

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:26.920
Cry all you like.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:29.330
Tears are the source of sadness.

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:34.270
The more tears you drain, the more sadness goes away.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:42.400
You'll eventually come to forget what's now causing your heart to ache.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:45.550
What's wrong?

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:52.370
If the tears dry up and the sadness disappears, I'll forget about Mom.

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:57.120
Forgetting about Mom... I don't want to.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:01.080
Did you...  lose your mother?

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.110
Mom!

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:22.570
Mom!  Mom!

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.640
<i>What are you looking up?</i>

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:43.050
<i>About cocoons.  I think it's a butterfly's cocoon.</i>

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:47.560
<i>It looks like this, and I want to know what the butterfly looks like.</i>

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:51.260
<i>I wonder what kind of butterfly will come out, too.</i>

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:54.620
<i>Yup.  But butterflies are strange.</i>

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:59.660
<i>They start as a caterpillar, then go on to a cocoon, and then change into a butterfly with such big wings.</i>

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.060
<i>You're right.</i>

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:07.600
<i>Erin, the butterfly inside a cocoon is very weak.</i>

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.210
<i>They are?</i>

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:17.860
<i>Inside the cocoon, a caterpillar completely melts its body, then reforms into a butterfly.</i>

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.620
<i>"Melts?"</i>

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:23.710
<i>Yes.  That's how they turn into a fully grown butterfly.</i>

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:25.750
<i>It's the same for humans.</i>

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:31.440
<i>When you decide to change, you slowly melt your heart,</i>

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:37.910
<i>and then, by becoming one with the world, you can adapt to live there.</i>

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:40.370
<i>Was that true for you, too?</i>

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:46.050
<i>Back when I first arrived in this village, I couldn't fit in well, either.</i>

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:53.710
<i>But a caterpillar that has become a cocoon will eventually become a butterfly and fly off.</i>

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:02.400
<i>That's how nature works.</i>

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.050
No!

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:12.570
Do you like butterflies?

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:23.600
Mom taught me that butterflies come out of their cocoons to fly and see the new world.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:30.500
You said you don't want to forget about your Mom, right?

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:33.970
You don't have to forget her.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:39.300
There <i>is</i> a today because there <i>were</i> all the good and bad things from before.

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:48.760
What's that?

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:49.980
It's huge, isn't it?

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:52.090
Ephon Noha.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:54.150
It's the mountain of the gods.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.950
It's the mountain that existed from the day this world began.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:59.340
Is Ephon Alma there, too?

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:03.490
Ephon Alma isn't anywhere in this world.

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:05.680
That's why it's called the afterworld.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:12.130
Strangely, it's said that only untainted people can reach it.

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:14.380
How about those who aren't?

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:17.010
They'll die and return to the soil.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.340
That's all.

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:26.570
But the memories from the days the person was alive remain in us.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.560
Same with your mother.

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:45.680
I'll hold back on asking why you came here and what happened to you until you feel like talking about it.

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:49.500
First, eat for the sake of living.

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:54.760
The bird that tried to eat the cocoon and the butterfly that survived both eat to live.

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:56.420
We live to eat.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:20:04.730
Then, you can take your time in finding what you will live for.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:06.290
Yes.

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:10.200
What is this?

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:12.040
It's called "pako."

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:13.200
"Pako?"

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.210
It's not made of rice.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:24.330
Yeah.  This is made by kneading ground wheat.

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:26.900
Around here, that's what we eat with all our meals.

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:28.120
Really?

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:30.580
Pour this on it.

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:34.380
It's what I've devoted my heart to making.

00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:40.820
You eat it...

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:44.780
like this.

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:00.960
How is it?  Isn't it good?

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:05.950
It's delicious!

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:08.710
There are plenty of seconds.

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:12.210
Eat a ton like me, and then you'll get your energy back.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.060
You farted.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:21.610
Excuse me.

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:23.300
Unknown land.

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:25.380
Unknown food.

00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:27.250
And Jone.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:31.940
Everything was something Erin was unfamiliar with.

00:23:32.990 --> 00:23:37.530
Even among all these, Erin recalled her mother's words:

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:42.090
"Live.  And find your happiness."

00:23:43.790 --> 00:23:49.790
She doesn't know what happiness is, nor how to truly live.

00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:55.840
But Erin thinks that she should start off by surviving.

00:24:02.400 --> 00:24:11.190
If you choose to live here as you try to come to terms with the sadness of losing your mother along with your tears,

00:24:11.190 --> 00:24:15.490
then you've got to learn how to keep bees, and to eat and sleep well.

00:24:16.060 --> 00:24:20.450
If that's all you need, then I'll teach you everything.

00:24:21.030 --> 00:24:24.960
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Honey and Erin.

00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:29.980
Honey and Erin
